      "writtenOn": "2025-02-27T18:36:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unrelated, but while we\u0027re on the topic of cleaning up the code:\n\nThis is declared as static, but we re-evaluate it on every invocation. I wonder if we should change that to only invoke `__has_memfd_support()` if `memfd_supported` is false? Otherwise, I don\u0027t think we should use `static` here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 160,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 160,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "fixSuggestions": [
        {
          "fixId": "9e9d7fb3_0dbaa1f0",
          "description": "prompt_to_edit API",
          "replacements": [
            {
              "path": "libcutils/ashmem-dev.cpp",
              "range": {
                "startLine": 160,
                "startChar": 0,
                "endLine": 162,
                "endChar": 0
              },
              "replacement": "    static bool has_memfd_support \u003d __has_memfd_support();\n    return has_memfd_support;\n"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "revId": "c026325ede55b6f336fcb1757a4c925c1373dd4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "46070a17_f483fd8c",
        "filename": "libcutils/ashmem-dev.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 160,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003224
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-02-27T18:44:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This is declared as static, but we re-evaluate it on every invocation.\n\nno, `static` means that we\u0027ll only evaluate this once, the first time it\u0027s called. it\u0027s even thread-safe because the compiler will insert the appropriate locking.\n\nsee the \"static initializers\" section of https://docs.google.com/document/d/1iIZfAd9lqgTt4Y3T6GzizidVn3Vco8YgxHLh3l6sLLg/edit?tab\u003dt.0#heading\u003dh.6aoknd5l5ens [googlers only :-( ]",
      "parentUuid": "6faad28c_9290aa88",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 160,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 160,
        "endChar": 56
      },
      "revId": "c026325ede55b6f336fcb1757a4c925c1373dd4f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
